cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DL-SplatGenerator"
message: "If you use this tool in a publication or in teaching, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Marc
    family-names: Ihle
    affiliation: "Digital Landscapes"
url: "https://digital-landscapes.com/"
abstract: >-
  Site video to a measurable splat scene. A browser viewer for Gaussian-splat
  scenes of landscapes and sites that measures rather than only shows: distances,
  heights and areas at a calibrated scale, section boxes, annotations and saved
  viewpoints, and still images of any of it. Behind it, an
  optional generator turns a walked phone video into camera poses, a splat
  scene, a dense measurable mesh and a ground-only terrain model that can be cut
  into laser sheets. It states its limits where it offers its results: a
  reconstruction is not a survey, it has no scale until one is given, and where
  planting hides the ground the ground is absent.
keywords:
  - landscape architecture
  - Gaussian splatting
  - photogrammetry
  - site survey
  - measurement
  - terrain model
  - digital fabrication
license: Apache-2.0
